// NEGATIVE TEST -- there is no `loop` keyword.
//
// `loop` lexes as an identifier, so `loop { ... }` parses as an expression
// statement whose expression is a variable named `loop`, and the `{` that
// follows is where a `;` was expected. The unconditional loop must be written
// `while true { ... }`.
fn main() {
    loop { break; }
}
